## The proposed default: the key VS Code users expect for each command
## where VS Code has a well-known single key, else the classic key, else a
## free Ctrl-Alt key, else the palette (`PALETTE_ONLY_IN_VSCODE`). Moved from
## classic: Ctrl-D adds the next occurrence (Duplicate line is
## Alt-Shift-Down), Ctrl-H replaces, Ctrl-Shift-T reopens a closed tab,
## Ctrl-Shift-K deletes the line, Ctrl-Shift-E reveals the file in the tree,
## Shift-F5 stops the job, Ctrl-Shift-O is the outline, Ctrl-Alt-Up and
## Down add carets (box selection adds Shift). F1 and F8 are left free: F1
## opens the palette (`palette_keys`) and F8 is next problem in VS Code,
## which this editor has no command for yet. A command may have two keys
## (Redo: Ctrl-Y and Ctrl-Shift-Z, as on macOS; Show jobs: Ctrl-` and Ctrl-J).
